                                "example_id": "5fa00ce4-7fd7-471f-a715-bbe223459151",
                                "sense_id": "e3686c54-1456-340f-8100-90c832957e38",
                                "text": "The wall text accompanying Warhol’s small canvas with 12 electric-blue crucifixes silkscreened on a black background suggests that the repetition of crosses mirrors his Campbell’s soup cans, with the religious icon serving as “a commodity to be bought and sold.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fd8d539d-0635-422f-8f8a-92bccc075f49",
                                "sense_id": "e3686c54-1456-340f-8100-90c832957e38",
                                "text": "A year ago, if anyone had told Toronto designer Kingi Carpenter she would soon be silkscreening a U. S. president onto dresses, hoodies and scarves, she would have laughed in their face."
                            }
